---

<section class="bg-slate-50 py-12 lg:py-16 border-t border-slate-200">
  <div class="section-container">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-10 text-center">Where conventional reviews fall short on BESS</h2>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <!-- Thermal management -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-sm border border-slate-200">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-red-100 rounded-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-5 h-5 text-red-600">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15.362 5.214A8.252 8.252 0 0112 21 8.25 8.25 0 016.038 7.048 8.287 8.287 0 009 9.6a8.983 8.983 0 013.361-6.867 8.21 8.21 0 003 2.48z" />
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 18a3.75 3.75 0 00.495-7.467 5.99 5.99 0 00-1.925 3.546 5.974 5.974 0 01-2.133-1A3.75 3.75 0 0012 18z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Thermal management & fire propagation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Certificate compliance is not the same as operational risk analysis. UL9540A fire propagation test results, thermal derating behavior at peak ambient temperature, and HVAC sizing against rated conditions are the first line of inquiry — not an afterthought.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Revenue stacking -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-sm border border-slate-200">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-amber-100 rounded-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-5 h-5 text-amber-600">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.25 18L9 11.25l4.306 4.307a11.95 11.95 0 015.814-5.519l2.74-1.22m0 0l-5.94-2.28m5.94 2.28l-2.28 5.941" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Revenue constraint under degradation</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            A battery's bankable value depends on its ability to participate in capacity, frequency regulation, and arbitrage markets over time. Degradation curves that are not project-specific undermine any revenue stacking model — regardless of the headline capacity.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Delivery path -->
        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-sm border border-slate-200">
          <div class="w-10 h-10 bg-slate-100 rounded-sm flex items-center justify-center mb-4">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" class="w-5 h-5 text-slate-600">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8.25 18.75a1.5 1.5 0 01-3 0m3 0a1.5 1.5 0 00-3 0m3 0h6m-9 0H3.375a1.125 1.125 0 01-1.125-1.125V14.25m17.25 4.5a1.5 1.5 0 01-3 0m3 0a1.5 1.5 0 00-3 0m3 0h1.125c.621 0 1.129-.504 1.09-1.124a17.902 17.902 0 00-3.213-9.193 2.056 2.056 0 00-1.58-.86H14.25M16.5 18.75h-2.25m0-11.177v-.958c0-.568-.422-1.048-.987-1.106a48.554 48.554 0 00-10.026 0 1.106 1.106 0 00-.987 1.106v7.635m12-6.677v6.677m0 4.5v-4.5m0 0h-12" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Delivery path and structural exposure</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Weight, access routes, and site preparation constraints are material before financial close — not during construction. Undisclosed logistics dependencies create execution exposure that no contract renegotiation resolves cleanly.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-center text-sm text-slate-500 mt-8 italic">
        These are not edge cases. They are the most common categories of Critical Silences identified across the project cohort evaluated to date.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
